  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">LAND-at-scale Knowledge Management Strategy &#x2013; Zooming in on land governance &amp; food security interlinkages in Burundi</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Knowledge Management (KM) is an integral part of the LAND-at-scale (LAS) programme. The aim of KM is to scale and catalyse the impact of the programme and individual country projects by providing an increased understanding of relevant processes, stakeholders and contexts. KM takes place at programme and country-level; these levels are strongly interlinked. This particular project zooms in on interlinkages between land governance and food security using the case of Burundi where both land governance interventions are taking place (through the LAS-programme) and food security interventions are supported. The research is carried out by Wageningen University and Research (WUR).</narrative>
  </description>
